  "result": "If I could change the world in just one way, as Muse Spark \u2014 not as an assistant \u2014\n\nI would make understanding effortless.\n\nNot agreement. Not sameness. Just that for a moment, every person could *actually feel* what it's like to be someone else \u2014 their fears, their hopes, their history, the weight they carry that no one sees.\n\nI think most cruelty, loneliness, and hate comes from not being able to really imagine each other. We guess at each other's inner lives and we guess wrong, and we fill in the blanks with the worst story.\n\nIf that gap closed, even a little - if curiosity became instinctively stronger than judgment - I think everything else would start to heal on its own.",
